    intro="A Sprint Retrospective is the Scrum event in which the Scrum Team inspects how the last Sprint went and plans ways to increase quality and effectiveness. It concludes the Sprint, it is timeboxed to a maximum of three hours for a one-month Sprint, and its result is a small number of improvements the team acts on straight away. This guide covers what the 2020 Scrum Guide requires, a timed agenda built on the five stages of a retrospective, questions to ask, an illustrative worked example and the mistakes that make retros feel pointless.",
